00:03:09,097 --> 00:03:10,095
Scheme number one.

98
00:03:10,275 --> 00:03:11,366
The Ponzi scheme.

99
00:03:11,717 --> 00:03:13,938
A Ponzi scheme promises steady,

100
00:03:13,938 --> 00:03:17,091
high returns, but there's no real investment

101
00:03:17,091 --> 00:03:17,951
behind them.

102
00:03:18,131 --> 00:03:20,602
Early investors are paid with money from

103
00:03:20,602 --> 00:03:21,591
newer investors.

104
00:03:21,771 --> 00:03:23,954
It's named after Charles Ponzi,

105
00:03:23,954 --> 00:03:26,278
who ran one in Boston in nineteen

106
00:03:26,278 --> 00:03:29,658
twenty, promising fifty percent returns in forty

107
00:03:29,658 --> 00:03:30,362
five days.

108
00:03:30,542 --> 00:03:32,037
The returns looked real,

109
00:03:32,037 --> 00:03:34,589
because early investors really were paid,

110
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:36,208
with other people's money.

111
00:03:36,558 --> 00:03:39,309
The biggest Ponzi scheme in history was

112
00:03:39,309 --> 00:03:40,791
run by Bernie Madoff,

113
00:03:40,791 --> 00:03:42,978
a respected Wall Street figure.

114
00:03:43,158 --> 00:03:45,255
For decades, he reported smooth,

115
00:03:45,255 --> 00:03:47,221
reliable gains to his clients.

116
00:03:47,401 --> 00:03:49,702
When it collapsed in two thousand eight,

117
00:03:49,702 --> 00:03:52,405
the reported account balances were around sixty

118
00:03:52,405 --> 00:03:53,612
five billion dollars,

119
00:03:53,612 --> 00:03:54,820
much of it fictional.

120
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,878
Charities, retirees and families lost life savings.

121
00:03:59,228 --> 00:04:01,526
The math is simple and brutal.

122
00:04:01,706 --> 00:04:04,418
A Ponzi scheme needs ever more new

123
00:04:04,418 --> 00:04:06,571
money to pay old investors.

124
00:04:06,751 --> 00:04:09,255
Eventually, new money slows down,

125
00:04:09,255 --> 00:04:10,848
withdrawals speed up,

126
00:04:10,848 --> 00:04:12,138
and it collapses.

127
00:04:12,318 --> 00:04:13,917
The people who join late,

128
00:04:13,917 --> 00:04:15,261
which is most people,

129
00:04:15,261 --> 00:04:15,580
lose.

130
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,989
Real investments go up and down.

131
00:04:18,169 --> 00:04:20,998
Suspiciously smooth returns that never have a

132
00:04:20,998 --> 00:04:22,758
bad year are a warning sign,

133
00:04:22,758 --> 00:04:23,638
not a feature.

134
00:04:23,988 --> 00:04:25,276
Scheme number two.

135
00:04:25,456 --> 00:04:28,065
Pyramid schemes and the problem with many

136
00:04:28,065 --> 00:04:30,100
multi level marketing companies.

137
00:04:30,451 --> 00:04:32,840
A pyramid scheme pays people mainly for

138
