256
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:30,592
Separate the hobby from the plan.

257
00:08:30,942 --> 00:08:33,196
In a study of Brazilian day traders

258
00:08:33,196 --> 00:08:35,901
who persisted for over three hundred days,

259
00:08:35,901 --> 00:08:38,349
about ninety seven percent lost money.

260
00:08:38,699 --> 00:08:39,918
Scheme number five.

261
00:08:40,098 --> 00:08:41,851
Sports betting as income.

262
00:08:42,201 --> 00:08:45,413
Since a twenty eighteen Supreme Court decision

263
00:08:45,413 --> 00:08:48,346
allowed states to legalize sports betting,

264
00:08:48,346 --> 00:08:50,721
it has exploded across much of the

265
00:08:50,721 --> 00:08:51,280
country.

266
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:53,070
Apps offer promotions,

267
00:08:53,070 --> 00:08:54,755
live bets during games,

268
00:08:54,755 --> 00:08:56,951
and parlays with huge payouts.

269
00:08:57,131 --> 00:08:58,613
Some people see it as a way

270
00:08:58,613 --> 00:09:00,423
to make money from what they know

271
00:09:00,423 --> 00:09:01,137
about sports.

272
00:09:01,487 --> 00:09:04,325
But sportsbooks build an edge into the

273
00:09:04,325 --> 00:09:06,342
odds, often called the vig,

274
00:09:06,342 --> 00:09:07,686
or the house edge.

275
00:09:07,866 --> 00:09:09,704
To break even on standard bets,

276
00:09:09,704 --> 00:09:11,483
you need to win more than half

277
00:09:11,483 --> 00:09:12,847
the time, consistently.

278
00:09:13,027 --> 00:09:14,918
Very few people can do that over

279
00:09:14,918 --> 00:09:15,686
the long run.

280
00:09:15,866 --> 00:09:18,554
And sportsbooks can limit accounts that win

281
00:09:18,554 --> 00:09:19,117
too much.

282
00:09:19,467 --> 00:09:22,623
Researchers have begun studying the financial effects

283
00:09:22,623 --> 00:09:24,053
of legal sports betting.

284
00:09:24,233 --> 00:09:26,984
Some early studies found signs of higher

285
00:09:26,984 --> 00:09:29,805
debt and financial stress in states after

286
00:09:29,805 --> 00:09:31,318
betting was legalized,

287
00:09:31,318 --> 00:09:33,451
particularly among younger men.

288
00:09:33,631 --> 00:09:35,834
It's entertainment with a cost,

289
00:09:35,834 --> 00:09:37,184
not an income plan.

290
00:09:37,534 --> 00:09:39,075
Try this: if you bet,

291
00:09:39,075 --> 00:09:41,645
set a strict monthly budget for it,

292
00:09:41,645 --> 00:09:43,333
like any entertainment,

293
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:45,022
and never chase losses.

294
00:09:45,202 --> 00:09:47,754
And if betting stops feeling like fun,

295
00:09:47,754 --> 00:09:50,372
the national problem gambling helpline,

296
00:09:50,372 --> 00:09:52,118
one eight hundred GAMBLER,

297
00:09:52,118 --> 00:09:54,200
offers free, confidential help.

298
00:09:54,550 --> 00:09:55,885
Those are the classics.

299
00:09:56,065 --> 00:09:58,514
The modern ones use something more powerful

300
00:09:58,514 --> 00:09:59,083
than math.

301
00:09:59,263 --> 00:10:00,854
They use your emotions.

302
00:10:01,204 --> 00:10:02,121
Angle two.

303
00:10:02,301 --> 00:10:03,415
The psychology.

304
00:10:03,595 --> 00:10:05,865
Five modern schemes built on hype,

305
00:10:05,865 --> 00:10:08,135
gurus and the fear of missing out.

306
00:10:08,485 --> 00:10:09,947
Scheme number six.

307
00:10:10,127 --> 00:10:11,254
The pump and dump.

308
00:10:11,604 --> 00:10:12,961
In a pump and dump,

309
00:10:12,961 --> 00:10:15,532
promoters buy a cheap stock or coin,

310
00:10:15,532 --> 00:10:17,246
then hype it everywhere.

311
00:10:17,426 --> 00:10:19,616
Social media, chat groups,

312
00:10:19,616 --> 00:10:21,048
paid influencers.

313
00:10:21,228 --> 00:10:23,387
The price shoots up as new buyers

314
00:10:23,387 --> 00:10:23,910
pile in.

315
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:25,737
Then the promoters sell,

316
00:10:25,737 --> 00:10:27,109
or dump, at the top.

317
00:10:27,289 --> 00:10:28,323
The price crashes,

318
00:10:28,323 --> 00:10:30,910
and the latecomers are left holding something

319
00:10:30,910 --> 00:10:31,944
worth very little.

320
00:10:32,295 --> 00:10:34,631
This used to happen with penny stocks

321
00:10:34,631 --> 00:10:36,904
through phone calls and spam emails.

322
00:10:37,084 --> 00:10:39,854
Today it happens with small crypto tokens

323
00:10:39,854 --> 00:10:42,894
and thinly traded stocks through social media

324
00:10:42,894 --> 00:10:44,178
and messaging apps.

325
00:10:44,358 --> 00:10:47,331
The Securities and Exchange Commission has brought

326
00:10:47,331 --> 00:10:50,186
many cases against people running these schemes.

327
00:10:50,536 --> 00:10:53,067
The psychology is fear of missing out.

328
00:10:53,247 --> 00:10:54,554
You see the price rising,

329
00:10:54,554 --> 00:10:55,966
you see people celebrating,

330
00:10:55,966 --> 00:10:57,692
and you jump in because you don't

331
00:10:57,692 --> 00:10:59,208
want to be the one who missed

332
00:10:59,208 --> 00:10:59,365
it.

333
00:10:59,545 --> 00:11:01,769
But by the time something is everywhere,

334
00:11:01,769 --> 00:11:03,994
the early buyers are often getting ready

335
00:11:03,994 --> 00:11:04,828
to sell to you.

336
00:11:05,178 --> 00:11:07,479
Try this: if someone is urging you

337
00:11:07,479 --> 00:11:09,307
to buy something right now,

338
00:11:09,307 --> 00:11:10,390
before it moons,

339
00:11:10,390 --> 00:11:12,353
ask, why are they telling me?

340
00:11:12,533 --> 00:11:13,841
If they already own it,

341
00:11:13,841 --> 00:11:15,319
they benefit when you buy.

342
00:11:15,499 --> 00:11:16,630
That's a conflict,

343
00:11:16,630 --> 00:11:18,390
and sometimes it's a scheme.

344
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:20,005
Scheme number seven.

345
00:11:20,185 --> 00:11:21,369
Joining a mania.

346
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,960
Manias aren't always scams.

347
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:27,363
Sometimes there's a real technology or asset

348
00:11:27,363 --> 00:11:28,169
underneath.

349
00:11:28,349 --> 00:11:31,028
But when prices rise mostly because people

350
00:11:31,028 --> 00:11:32,751
expect them to keep rising,

351
00:11:32,751 --> 00:11:34,409
it can turn into a bubble.

352
00:11:34,589 --> 00:11:36,357
History is full of them,

353
00:11:36,357 --> 00:11:39,376
from tulip bulbs in the sixteen hundreds,

354
00:11:39,376 --> 00:11:42,174
to dot com stocks around two thousand,

355
00:11:42,174 --> 00:11:44,605
to the NFT craze of twenty twenty

356
00:11:44,605 --> 00:11:44,899
one.

357
00:11:45,249 --> 00:11:46,694
In twenty twenty one,

358
00:11:46,694 --> 00:11:48,483
some digital collectibles,

359
00:11:48,483 --> 00:11:50,891
NFTs, sold for millions of dollars.

360
00:11:51,071 --> 00:11:52,727
Within a couple of years,

361
00:11:52,727 --> 00:11:55,575
trading volumes had collapsed and many NFTs

362
00:11:55,575 --> 00:11:57,892
were worth a tiny fraction of their

363
00:11:57,892 --> 00:11:58,687
peak prices.

364
00:11:58,867 --> 00:12:00,879
The people who bought near the top,

365
00:12:00,879 --> 00:12:03,179
often with money they couldn't afford to

366
00:12:03,179 --> 00:12:04,788
lose, took the biggest hits.

367
00:12:05,139 --> 00:12:08,018
The psychological driver is social proof.

368
00:12:08,198 --> 00:12:10,687
When everyone around you is making money,

369
00:12:10,687 --> 00:12:12,447
it feels foolish not to join.

370
00:12:12,627 --> 00:12:15,405
Your neighbor, your coworker and your cousin

371
00:12:15,405 --> 00:12:17,236
are all bragging about gains.

372
00:12:17,416 --> 00:12:19,239
Nobody brags about losses,

373
00:12:19,239 --> 00:12:21,062
so you only hear one side.

374
00:12:21,412 --> 00:12:23,160
Try this: when you hear about a

375
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:25,303
new thing that's making everyone rich,

376
00:12:25,303 --> 00:12:27,220
write down the date and the price,

377
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:29,701
and wait three months before doing anything.

378
00:12:29,881 --> 00:12:31,950
You'll learn more from watching than from

379
00:12:31,950 --> 00:12:32,505
jumping in.

380
00:12:32,855 --> 00:12:33,958
Scheme number eight.

381
00:12:34,138 --> 00:12:35,415
The trading course.

382
00:12:35,765 --> 00:12:37,611
You've seen the ads.

383
00:12:37,791 --> 00:12:39,980
A young person with a sports car,

384
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:41,373
a beach and a laptop,

385
00:12:41,373 --> 00:12:44,292
promising to teach you their trading system.

386
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:45,881
For a few hundred or a few

387
00:12:45,881 --> 00:12:48,211
thousand dollars, you can learn the secret.

388
00:12:48,391 --> 00:12:51,012
Often with a monthly membership for signals

389
00:12:51,012 --> 00:12:52,535
and a private chat group.

390
00:12:52,886 --> 00:12:54,441
Here's the question to ask.

391
00:12:54,621 --> 00:12:56,691
If the system reliably made lots of

392
00:12:56,691 --> 00:12:58,464
money, why would they sell it?

393
00:12:58,644 --> 00:12:59,826
The honest answer,

394
00:12:59,826 --> 00:13:00,746
in many cases,

395
00:13:00,746 --> 00:13:03,044
is that the course is the business.

396
00:13:03,224 --> 00:13:06,461
Selling courses to thousands of people produces

397
00:13:06,461 --> 00:13:10,318
steady income, while trading produces uncertain results.

398
00:13:10,668 --> 00:13:13,856
Regulators have taken action against some trading

399
00:13:13,856 --> 00:13:16,914
educators for misleading claims about earnings.

400
00:13:17,094 --> 00:13:19,073
And the lifestyle in the ads is

401
00:13:19,073 --> 00:13:20,159
sometimes rented.

402
00:13:20,339 --> 00:13:21,496
The car, the house,

403
00:13:21,496 --> 00:13:22,835
the private jet photo.

404
00:13:23,015 --> 00:13:24,478
The goal is to make you feel

405
00:13:24,478 --> 00:13:25,627
that success is close,

406
00:13:25,627 --> 00:13:27,247
and that the course is the only

407
00:13:27,247 --> 00:13:28,135
thing in the way.

408
00:13:28,485 --> 00:13:31,369
Try this: before buying any course that

409
00:13:31,369 --> 00:13:34,772
promises income, search the person's name with

410
00:13:34,772 --> 00:13:36,325
words like complaint,

411
00:13:36,325 --> 00:13:37,657
lawsuit or refund.

412
00:13:37,837 --> 00:13:40,743
And remember, real investing education,

413
00:13:40,743 --> 00:13:42,680
like how index funds work,

414
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:45,586
is available for free from sources like

415
00:13:45,586 --> 00:13:48,344
the SEC's investor education website.

416
00:13:48,694 --> 00:13:49,855
Scheme number nine.

417
00:13:50,035 --> 00:13:51,230
The free seminar.

418
00:13:51,581 --> 00:13:53,723
Free real estate seminars,

419
00:13:53,723 --> 00:13:55,536
free wealth workshops,

420
00:13:55,536 --> 00:13:56,608
free dinners.

421
00:13:56,788 --> 00:13:58,866
They usually end with an upsell.

422
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:00,584
A mentoring program,

423
00:14:00,584 --> 00:14:03,662
an advanced course or a coaching package

424
00:14:03,662 --> 00:14:05,508
that can cost thousands,

425
00:14:05,508 --> 00:14:08,508
sometimes tens of thousands of dollars.

426
00:14:08,688 --> 00:14:10,348
The free event is the funnel.

427
00:14:10,699 --> 00:14:13,217
The most famous example may be Trump

428
00:14:13,217 --> 00:14:16,715
University, which offered real estate seminars and

429
00:14:16,715 --> 00:14:18,744
expensive mentoring packages.

430
00:14:18,924 --> 00:14:20,206
Former students sued,

431
00:14:20,206 --> 00:14:21,670
saying they were misled,

432
00:14:21,670 --> 00:14:23,927
and in twenty sixteen a settlement of

433
00:14:23,927 --> 00:14:26,367
twenty five million dollars was reached,

434
00:14:26,367 --> 00:14:28,503
without an admission of wrongdoing.

435
00:14:28,683 --> 00:14:31,634
Many other seminar companies have faced similar

436
00:14:31,634 --> 00:14:33,454
complaints and legal actions.

437
00:14:33,805 --> 00:14:37,248
Seminars use a powerful set of persuasion

438
00:14:37,248 --> 00:14:37,752
tools.

439
00:14:37,932 --> 00:14:39,997
Free food creates a feeling that you

440
00:14:39,997 --> 00:14:40,800
owe something.

441
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:43,499
Limited time discounts create urgency.

442
00:14:43,679 --> 00:14:46,338
Success stories create social proof.

443
00:14:46,518 --> 00:14:48,642
And the high price itself makes the

444
00:14:48,642 --> 00:14:49,978
product feel valuable.

445
00:14:50,328 --> 00:14:52,376
Try this: go to any free seminar

446
00:14:52,376 --> 00:14:54,681
with your credit cards left at home.

447
00:14:54,861 --> 00:14:56,998
Take notes, then wait at least a

448
00:14:56,998 --> 00:14:58,867
week before buying anything.

449
00:14:59,047 --> 00:15:00,606
If it's truly valuable,

450
00:15:00,606 --> 00:15:02,437
it will still be available.

451
00:15:02,787 --> 00:15:03,878
Scheme number ten.

452
00:15:04,058 --> 00:15:06,229
The easy passive income business.

453
00:15:06,579 --> 00:15:08,926
Dropshipping, print on demand,

454
00:15:08,926 --> 00:15:10,804
automated online stores,

455
00:15:10,804 --> 00:15:13,777
affiliate empires, YouTube automation.

456
00:15:13,957 --> 00:15:15,833
Sellers promise that you can set it

457
00:15:15,833 --> 00:15:17,602
up once and earn while you sleep.

458
00:15:17,782 --> 00:15:21,037
Some people really do build real businesses

459
00:15:21,037 --> 00:15:21,718
this way.

460
00:15:21,898 --> 00:15:23,743
But it's almost never fast,

461
00:15:23,743 --> 00:15:24,835
easy or passive.

462
00:15:25,186 --> 00:15:27,866
Real online businesses need marketing,

463
00:15:27,866 --> 00:15:30,265
customer service, product quality,

464
00:15:30,265 --> 00:15:32,593
returns, and constant adjustment.

465
00:15:32,773 --> 00:15:35,431
Advertising costs can eat the profits.

466
00:15:35,611 --> 00:15:37,004
Competition is fierce,

467
00:15:37,004 --> 00:15:39,473
because the same course taught the same

468
00:15:39,473 --> 00:15:42,005
strategy to thousands of other people at

469
00:15:42,005 --> 00:15:42,891
the same time.

470
00:15:43,241 --> 00:15:45,609
The scheme isn't the business model itself.

471
00:15:45,789 --> 00:15:47,762
It's the promise that it's easy,

472
00:15:47,762 --> 00:15:50,229
and the expensive course or software you

473
00:15:50,229 --> 00:15:51,339
need to buy first.

474
00:15:51,519 --> 00:15:54,331
The people reliably earning passive income are

475
00:15:54,331 --> 00:15:56,348
often the ones selling the dream.

476
00:15:56,699 --> 00:15:58,803
Try this: if you want to start

477
00:15:58,803 --> 00:16:00,136
an online business,

478
00:16:00,136 --> 00:16:01,679
start small and cheap.

479
00:16:01,859 --> 00:16:04,232
Test one idea with your own effort

480
00:16:04,232 --> 00:16:06,954
and a small budget before paying anyone

481
00:16:06,954 --> 00:16:07,862
for a system.

482
00:16:08,042 --> 00:16:10,495
Real businesses grow from real customers,

483
00:16:10,495 --> 00:16:11,931
not from course modules.

484
00:16:12,281 --> 00:16:13,326
Quick pause.

485
00:16:13,506 --> 00:16:15,785
If this video might protect someone you

486
00:16:15,785 --> 00:16:17,596
love from one of these schemes,

487
00:16:17,596 --> 00:16:18,707
share it with them.

488
00:16:18,887 --> 00:16:20,689
And subscribe to the channel if it's

489
00:16:20,689 --> 00:16:21,290
helping you.

490
00:16:21,470 --> 00:16:23,467
It's free, and it helps me keep

491
00:16:23,467 --> 00:16:24,756
making these videos.

492
00:16:24,936 --> 00:16:26,509
Now, the newest scams,

493
00:16:26,509 --> 00:16:28,512
and how to protect yourself.

494
00:16:28,862 --> 00:16:29,756
Angle three.

495
00:16:29,936 --> 00:16:31,862
Five scams of the internet age,

496
00:16:31,862 --> 00:16:33,976
and the checklist that stops them.

497
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:35,614
Scheme number eleven.

498
00:16:35,794 --> 00:16:36,781
Pig butchering.

499
00:16:37,131 --> 00:16:38,414
The name is ugly,

500
00:16:38,414 --> 00:16:39,847
and so is the scam.

501
00:16:40,027 --> 00:16:42,415
It often starts with a wrong number

502
00:16:42,415 --> 00:16:44,394
text, a dating app match or a

503
00:16:44,394 --> 00:16:46,645
friendly message on social media.

504
00:16:46,825 --> 00:16:48,349
Over weeks or months,

505
00:16:48,349 --> 00:16:50,163
the scammer builds trust,

506
00:16:50,163 --> 00:16:51,469
sometimes romance.

507
00:16:51,649 --> 00:16:53,938
Then they mention how they've been making

508
00:16:53,938 --> 00:16:55,390
money investing in crypto,

509
00:16:55,390 --> 00:16:56,618
and offer to show you.

510
00:16:56,968 --> 00:16:59,119
They direct you to a fake investment

511
00:16:59,119 --> 00:17:00,613
platform that looks real.

512
00:17:00,793 --> 00:17:02,173
You invest a little,

513
00:17:02,173 --> 00:17:04,450
and the platform shows big gains.

514
00:17:04,630 --> 00:17:07,308
You might even withdraw a small amount,

515
00:17:07,308 --> 00:17:08,613
which builds trust.

516
00:17:08,793 --> 00:17:10,035
So you invest more.

517
00:17:10,215 --> 00:17:12,708
When you try to withdraw the larger

518
00:17:12,708 --> 00:17:14,774
sum, there are suddenly fees,

519
00:17:14,774 --> 00:17:15,985
taxes or excuses.

520
00:17:16,165 --> 00:17:17,941
Then the person disappears.

521
00:17:18,292 --> 00:17:21,377
The FBI's Internet Crime Complaint Center has

522
00:17:21,377 --> 00:17:23,503
reported that investment fraud,

523
00:17:23,503 --> 00:17:25,971
much of it involving cryptocurrency,

524
00:17:25,971 --> 00:17:29,056
causes billions of dollars in reported losses

525
00:17:29,056 --> 00:17:31,525
every year, more than any other type

526
00:17:31,525 --> 00:17:32,827
of crime it tracks.

527
00:17:33,007 --> 00:17:35,996
Victims include people of every age and

528
00:17:35,996 --> 00:17:37,222
education level.

529
00:17:37,572 --> 00:17:40,182
Try this: never invest through a platform

530
00:17:40,182 --> 00:17:43,110
recommended by someone you've only met online,

531
00:17:43,110 --> 00:17:45,211
no matter how long you've talked.

532
00:17:45,391 --> 00:17:47,698
Never send money to someone you haven't

533
00:17:47,698 --> 00:17:48,526
met in person.

534
00:17:48,706 --> 00:17:50,930
And if you've been targeted,

535
00:17:50,930 --> 00:17:53,710
report it at the FBI's IC3 website.

536
00:17:54,060 --> 00:17:55,337
Scheme number twelve.

537
00:17:55,517 --> 00:17:56,956
The AI trading bot.

538
00:17:57,307 --> 00:18:00,108
Every new technology brings new scams that

539
00:18:00,108 --> 00:18:00,975
use its name.

540
00:18:01,155 --> 00:18:03,605
Today, it's artificial intelligence.

541
00:18:03,785 --> 00:18:06,138
Ads promise an AI trading bot that

542
00:18:06,138 --> 00:18:08,284
makes guaranteed daily profits,

543
00:18:08,284 --> 00:18:11,053
or a quantum algorithm that never loses.

544
00:18:11,233 --> 00:18:14,440
Regulators, including the SEC and the Commodity

545
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:16,283
Futures Trading Commission,

546
00:18:16,283 --> 00:18:19,081
have warned investors about these claims.

547
00:18:19,432 --> 00:18:21,712
Some of these are simply Ponzi schemes

548
00:18:21,712 --> 00:18:22,973
with modern branding.

549
00:18:23,153 --> 00:18:25,534
Others are fake platforms that never invest

550
00:18:25,534 --> 00:18:26,531
your money at all.

551
00:18:26,711 --> 00:18:29,797
Many use deepfake videos of celebrities or

552
00:18:29,797 --> 00:18:32,957
famous investors appearing to endorse them.

553
00:18:33,308 --> 00:18:34,923
The truth is that if an AI

554
00:18:34,923 --> 00:18:37,658
system reliably produced guaranteed profits,

555
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:39,771
its owners would have no reason to

556
00:18:39,771 --> 00:18:41,511
sell it to you for a monthly

557
00:18:41,511 --> 00:18:41,760
fee.

558
00:18:41,940 --> 00:18:44,362
Big financial firms do use algorithms,

559
00:18:44,362 --> 00:18:46,466
but they don't guarantee profits,

560
00:18:46,466 --> 00:18:49,080
and they don't advertise on social media.

561
00:18:49,430 --> 00:18:51,897
Try this: whenever you see the words

562
00:18:51,897 --> 00:18:54,091
guaranteed and returns together,

563
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:54,433
stop.

564
00:18:54,613 --> 00:18:57,484
Legitimate investments always carry risk,

565
00:18:57,484 --> 00:18:59,165
and honest firms say so.

566
00:18:59,515 --> 00:19:01,105
Scheme number thirteen.

567
00:19:01,285 --> 00:19:03,572
The guaranteed high yield investment.

568
00:19:03,923 --> 00:19:06,430
This scheme often targets retirees.

569
00:19:06,610 --> 00:19:08,033
A promissory note,

570
00:19:08,033 --> 00:19:10,801
a private fund or a special program

571
00:19:10,801 --> 00:19:13,726
that promises ten or twelve percent a

572
00:19:13,726 --> 00:19:16,177
year, guaranteed, with no risk.

573
00:19:16,357 --> 00:19:18,951
It's often sold by a friendly agent,

574
00:19:18,951 --> 00:19:19,816
at a church,

575
00:19:19,816 --> 00:19:22,626
a club, or through a trusted community.

576
00:19:22,977 --> 00:19:26,046
The SEC and state securities regulators have

577
00:19:26,046 --> 00:19:29,464
repeatedly warned about promissory note fraud and

578
00:19:29,464 --> 00:19:31,208
unregistered investments.

579
00:19:31,388 --> 00:19:34,048
Often, the investment isn't registered,

580
00:19:34,048 --> 00:19:35,821
the seller isn't licensed,

581
00:19:35,821 --> 00:19:38,071
and the returns are paid from new

582
00:19:38,071 --> 00:19:41,140
investors' money, a Ponzi scheme in disguise.

583
00:19:41,491 --> 00:19:44,454
Try this: before investing in anything,

584
00:19:44,454 --> 00:19:47,569
check the seller on FINRA BrokerCheck and

585
00:19:47,569 --> 00:19:51,749
the SEC's Investment Adviser Public Disclosure website,

586
00:19:51,749 --> 00:19:52,508
both free.

587
00:19:52,688 --> 00:19:55,497
And check whether the investment is registered

588
00:19:55,497 --> 00:19:57,755
with the SEC or your state securities

589
00:19:57,755 --> 00:19:58,366
regulator.

590
00:19:58,716 --> 00:20:00,150
And remember that safe,

591
00:20:00,150 --> 00:20:02,958
insured products already exist for people who

592
00:20:02,958 --> 00:20:03,894
want stability.

593
00:20:04,074 --> 00:20:07,799
Treasury bonds, FDIC insured savings accounts and

594
00:20:07,799 --> 00:20:09,623
certificates of deposit.

595
00:20:09,803 --> 00:20:11,963
They won't pay ten percent guaranteed.

596
00:20:12,143 --> 00:20:13,605
That's exactly the point.

597
00:20:13,785 --> 00:20:16,433
Real safety comes with modest returns.

598
00:20:16,613 --> 00:20:19,024
If someone offers both high returns and

599
00:20:19,024 --> 00:20:22,302
total safety, they're offering something that doesn't

600
00:20:22,302 --> 00:20:22,673
exist.

601
00:20:23,023 --> 00:20:24,509
Scheme number fourteen.

602
00:20:24,689 --> 00:20:27,173
Gifting circles and blessing looms.

603
00:20:27,524 --> 00:20:30,200
These schemes spread through friends and social

604
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:30,542
media.

605
00:20:30,722 --> 00:20:31,708
You give money,

606
00:20:31,708 --> 00:20:34,336
say one hundred or one thousand dollars,

607
00:20:34,336 --> 00:20:36,241
to someone at the center of a

608
00:20:36,241 --> 00:20:36,701
circle.

609
00:20:36,881 --> 00:20:38,257
Then you recruit others,

610
00:20:38,257 --> 00:20:40,378
and eventually you move to the center

611
00:20:40,378 --> 00:20:42,613
and receive gifts worth many times what

612
00:20:42,613 --> 00:20:43,244
you put in.

613
00:20:43,594 --> 00:20:45,774
It's a pyramid scheme dressed up as

614
00:20:45,774 --> 00:20:47,332
community and generosity.

615
00:20:47,512 --> 00:20:49,338
The math is the same as scheme

616
00:20:49,338 --> 00:20:50,008
number two.

617
00:20:50,188 --> 00:20:52,380
The circles need endless new members,

618
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:54,453
and most people who join lose their

619
00:20:54,453 --> 00:20:54,809
money.

620
00:20:54,989 --> 00:20:57,262
Regulators have warned that calling it a

621
00:20:57,262 --> 00:20:58,797
gift doesn't make it legal.

622
00:20:59,147 --> 00:21:02,054
Try this: if an opportunity requires you

623
00:21:02,054 --> 00:21:04,234
to recruit others to get paid,

624
00:21:04,234 --> 00:21:07,069
and there's no real product being sold,

625
00:21:07,069 --> 00:21:07,796
walk away.

626
00:21:07,976 --> 00:21:10,140
And gently warn the friend who invited

627
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:10,368
you.

628
00:21:10,548 --> 00:21:11,964
They may be a victim too.

629
00:21:12,314 --> 00:21:15,100
These circles can also damage friendships for

630
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:15,471
years.

631
00:21:15,651 --> 00:21:17,223
When the circle collapses,

632
00:21:17,223 --> 00:21:19,882
the people who recruited their friends often

633
00:21:19,882 --> 00:21:21,816
feel responsible for the losses.

634
00:21:21,996 --> 00:21:23,107
The money is gone,

635
00:21:23,107 --> 00:21:24,342
and so is the trust.

636
00:21:24,522 --> 00:21:26,847
It's one more reason why schemes that

637
00:21:26,847 --> 00:21:28,922
run on friendship are so harmful.

638
00:21:29,272 --> 00:21:30,816
Scheme number fifteen.

639
00:21:30,996 --> 00:21:32,203
The recovery scam.

640
00:21:32,553 --> 00:21:34,236
This is one of the cruelest.

641
00:21:34,416 --> 00:21:36,755
After someone loses money to a scam,

642
00:21:36,755 --> 00:21:39,418
they're contacted by a person claiming to

643
00:21:39,418 --> 00:21:40,198
be a lawyer,

644
00:21:40,198 --> 00:21:42,926
an investigator or even a government agent

645
00:21:42,926 --> 00:21:44,745
who can recover their money,

646
00:21:44,745 --> 00:21:45,980
for an upfront fee.

647
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:47,851
It's often the same scammers,

648
00:21:47,851 --> 00:21:48,901
or their partners,

649
00:21:48,901 --> 00:21:50,943
targeting the victim a second time.

650
00:21:51,293 --> 00:21:53,665
The FTC and FBI have warned that

651
00:21:53,665 --> 00:21:57,447
legitimate government agencies don't charge fees to

652
00:21:57,447 --> 00:21:58,856
recover lost money,

653
00:21:58,856 --> 00:22:01,822
and won't contact you asking for payment

654
00:22:01,822 --> 00:22:02,860
in gift cards,

655
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:04,714
crypto or wire transfers.

656
00:22:05,064 --> 00:22:08,147
Try this: if you've lost money to

657
00:22:08,147 --> 00:22:11,231
a scam, report it directly to the

658
00:22:11,231 --> 00:22:14,128
FTC at report fraud dot FTC dot

659
00:22:14,128 --> 00:22:16,557
gov, and to the FBI's IC3.

660
00:22:16,737 --> 00:22:18,943
Contact your bank immediately.

661
00:22:19,123 --> 00:22:21,661
And be extremely skeptical of anyone who

662
00:22:21,661 --> 00:22:23,946
contacts you offering to get it back

663
00:22:23,946 --> 00:22:24,580
for a fee.

664
00:22:24,930 --> 00:22:26,604
And if you've been scammed,

665
00:22:26,604 --> 00:22:27,658
please know this.

666
00:22:27,838 --> 00:22:29,524
It is not your fault that someone

667
00:22:29,524 --> 00:22:30,137
lied to you.

668
00:22:30,317 --> 00:22:33,041
Scammers are professionals who do this all

669
00:22:33,041 --> 00:22:33,300
day.

670
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:37,098
Reporting helps investigators find patterns and sometimes

671
00:22:37,098 --> 00:22:39,701
recover money, and talking about it helps

672
00:22:39,701 --> 00:22:41,224
protect the next person.

673
00:22:41,575 --> 00:22:44,006
Here's the checklist that catches nearly every

674
00:22:44,006 --> 00:22:45,116
scheme in this video.

675
00:22:45,296 --> 00:22:46,608
Ten red flags.

676
00:22:46,788 --> 00:22:48,721
If you see two or more,

677
00:22:48,721 --> 00:22:49,562
walk away.

678
00:22:49,913 --> 00:22:50,830
Red flag one.

679
00:22:51,010 --> 00:22:53,835
Guaranteed high returns with little or no

680
00:22:53,835 --> 00:22:54,179
risk.

681
00:22:54,359 --> 00:22:55,532
Red flag two.

682
00:22:55,712 --> 00:22:57,233
Pressure to act right now.

683
00:22:57,413 --> 00:22:58,713
Red flag three.

684
00:22:58,893 --> 00:23:01,424
You make money mainly by recruiting others.

685
00:23:01,604 --> 00:23:02,765
Red flag four.

686
00:23:02,945 --> 00:23:04,575
Payment by gift card,

687
00:23:04,575 --> 00:23:07,368
wire transfer or crypto to a person.

688
00:23:07,719 --> 00:23:08,914
Red flag five.

689
00:23:09,094 --> 00:23:11,399
The seller isn't registered or licensed,

690
00:23:11,399 --> 00:23:13,645
and you can't find them on BrokerCheck.

691
00:23:13,825 --> 00:23:15,195
Red flag six.

692
00:23:15,375 --> 00:23:17,909
Returns that are suspiciously smooth,

693
00:23:17,909 --> 00:23:18,731
every month.

694
00:23:18,911 --> 00:23:20,118
Red flag seven.

695
00:23:20,298 --> 00:23:22,292
You can't clearly explain how the money

696
00:23:22,292 --> 00:23:22,701
is made.

697
00:23:23,052 --> 00:23:24,201
Red flag eight.

698
00:23:24,381 --> 00:23:26,512
You were contacted out of the blue,

699
00:23:26,512 --> 00:23:27,609
especially online.

700
00:23:27,789 --> 00:23:28,915
Red flag nine.

701
00:23:29,095 --> 00:23:31,928
Celebrity endorsements you can't verify.

702
00:23:32,108 --> 00:23:33,361
And red flag ten.

703
00:23:33,541 --> 00:23:35,551
Fees appear when you try to withdraw

704
00:23:35,551 --> 00:23:36,165
your money.

705
00:23:36,345 --> 00:23:37,873
If you see any of these,

706
00:23:37,873 --> 00:23:40,037
stop and talk to someone you trust

707
00:23:40,037 --> 00:23:42,011
before sending a single dollar.

708
00:23:42,361 --> 00:23:43,881
Guaranteed returns.

709
00:23:44,061 --> 00:23:44,572
Pressure.

710
00:23:44,752 --> 00:23:45,333
Recruiting.

711
00:23:45,513 --> 00:23:47,382
Gift cards or crypto.

712
00:23:47,562 --> 00:23:48,793
Unlicensed seller.

713
00:23:48,973 --> 00:23:50,273
Smooth returns.

714
00:23:50,453 --> 00:23:51,475
Unclear model.

715
00:23:51,655 --> 00:23:53,129
Unsolicited contact.

716
00:23:53,309 --> 00:23:54,551
Fake celebrities.

717
00:23:54,731 --> 00:23:55,869
Withdrawal fees.

718
00:23:56,220 --> 00:23:58,229
So if get rich quick doesn't work,

719
00:23:58,229 --> 00:23:58,820
what does?

720
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,370
The answer is boring.

721
00:24:00,550 --> 00:24:02,373
And that's exactly why it works.

722
00:24:02,723 --> 00:24:03,895
Get rich slowly.

723
00:24:04,075 --> 00:24:05,422
Spend less than you earn.

724
00:24:05,602 --> 00:24:07,181
Build an emergency fund.

725
00:24:07,361 --> 00:24:08,975
Avoid high interest debt.

726
00:24:09,155 --> 00:24:11,812
Invest consistently in diversified,

727
00:24:11,812 --> 00:24:12,951
low cost funds,

728
00:24:12,951 --> 00:24:14,925
and hold them for decades.

729
00:24:15,105 --> 00:24:17,876
Increase your income through skills and career

730
00:24:17,876 --> 00:24:18,298
growth.

731
00:24:18,478 --> 00:24:19,813
None of it is exciting.

732
00:24:19,993 --> 00:24:22,111
All of it is available to ordinary

733
00:24:22,111 --> 00:24:22,547
people.

734
00:24:22,897 --> 00:24:24,693
Five hundred dollars a month,

735
00:24:24,693 --> 00:24:27,296
invested at a seven percent average yearly

736
00:24:27,296 --> 00:24:28,783
return for thirty years.

737
00:24:28,963 --> 00:24:31,246
You'd put in one hundred eighty thousand

738
00:24:31,246 --> 00:24:31,703
dollars.

739
00:24:31,883 --> 00:24:33,307
That's the slow path,

740
00:24:33,307 --> 00:24:35,681
and it's far more reliable than any

741
00:24:35,681 --> 00:24:36,155
scheme.

742
00:24:36,506 --> 00:24:38,057
That's an illustration,

743
00:24:38,057 --> 00:24:39,002
not a promise.

744
00:24:39,182 --> 00:24:40,710
Markets go up and down,

745
00:24:40,710 --> 00:24:42,305
and there are bad years.

746
00:24:42,485 --> 00:24:44,845
But notice that this path doesn't need

747
00:24:44,845 --> 00:24:45,838
you to be lucky,

748
00:24:45,838 --> 00:24:46,583
to be early,

749
00:24:46,583 --> 00:24:47,825
or to find a secret.

750
00:24:48,005 --> 00:24:50,548
It just needs time and consistency.

751
00:24:50,728 --> 00:24:52,898
Every scheme in this video is selling

752
00:24:52,898 --> 00:24:55,186
you a shortcut around those two things.

753
00:24:55,366 --> 00:24:56,190
There isn't one.

754
00:24:56,541 --> 00:24:58,514
Let's do some quick math on the

755
00:24:58,514 --> 00:25:00,042
returns schemes promise,

756
00:25:00,042 --> 00:25:02,206
because it exposes them instantly.

757
00:25:02,557 --> 00:25:04,820
Many scams promise one percent a day.

758
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:06,150
It sounds modest.

759
00:25:06,330 --> 00:25:07,305
One percent.

760
00:25:07,485 --> 00:25:09,511
But compounded daily for a year,

761
00:25:09,511 --> 00:25:11,791
one percent a day turns one thousand

762
00:25:11,791 --> 00:25:15,020
dollars into roughly thirty seven thousand dollars.

763
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:16,994
If that were real and repeatable,

764
00:25:16,994 --> 00:25:19,006
a few thousand dollars would make you

765
00:25:19,006 --> 00:25:20,854
one of the richest people on Earth

766
00:25:20,854 --> 00:25:21,887
within a few years.

767
00:25:22,067 --> 00:25:23,298
That's how you know it isn't.

768
00:25:23,648 --> 00:25:27,039
Charles Ponzi promised fifty percent in forty

769
00:25:27,039 --> 00:25:27,792
five days.

770
00:25:27,972 --> 00:25:30,616
Some modern schemes promise ten percent a

771
00:25:30,616 --> 00:25:31,003
month.

772
00:25:31,183 --> 00:25:33,755
Compare that with the long run average

773
00:25:33,755 --> 00:25:35,312
of broad stock markets,

774
00:25:35,312 --> 00:25:37,613
often cited at around seven to ten

775
00:25:37,613 --> 00:25:39,779
percent a year before inflation,

776
00:25:39,779 --> 00:25:42,081
with plenty of bad years along the

777
00:25:42,081 --> 00:25:42,351
way.

778
00:25:42,531 --> 00:25:44,630
When someone promises in a month what

779
00:25:44,630 --> 00:25:47,127
the market historically delivered in a year,

780
00:25:47,127 --> 00:25:47,864
with no risk,

781
00:25:47,864 --> 00:25:50,020
the numbers are telling you the truth.

782
00:25:50,370 --> 00:25:52,703
One percent a day sounds small.

783
00:25:52,883 --> 00:25:54,183
Compounded for a year,

784
00:25:54,183 --> 00:25:56,488
it would turn one thousand dollars into

785
00:25:56,488 --> 00:25:58,142
about thirty seven thousand.

786
00:25:58,322 --> 00:26:00,575
That's why no real investment offers it.

787
00:26:00,925 --> 00:26:02,213
Here's a simple rule.

788
00:26:02,393 --> 00:26:04,664
If the promised return is far above

789
00:26:04,664 --> 00:26:07,519
what the broad stock market has historically

790
00:26:07,519 --> 00:26:09,855
earned, and the seller says the risk

791
00:26:09,855 --> 00:26:10,829
is low or zero,

792
00:26:10,829 --> 00:26:12,970
one of those two claims is false.

793
00:26:13,150 --> 00:26:13,986
Usually both.

794
00:26:14,336 --> 00:26:16,031
Let's talk about why smart,

795
00:26:16,031 --> 00:26:18,794
careful people still fall for these schemes.

796
00:26:18,974 --> 00:26:20,518
It's not about intelligence.

797
00:26:20,868 --> 00:26:22,098
First, trust.

798
00:26:22,278 --> 00:26:24,623
Most schemes spread through people we trust.

799
00:26:24,803 --> 00:26:26,858
A friend, a church member,

800
00:26:26,858 --> 00:26:29,071
a coworker, a family member,

801
00:26:29,071 --> 00:26:32,154
or someone we've been talking to online

802
00:26:32,154 --> 00:26:33,023
for months.

803
00:26:33,203 --> 00:26:35,374
Scammers call this affinity fraud.

804
00:26:35,554 --> 00:26:38,051
They target communities where trust is high

805
00:26:38,051 --> 00:26:39,444
and questions feel rude.

806
00:26:39,794 --> 00:26:41,071
Second, stress.

807
00:26:41,251 --> 00:26:43,156
People facing money problems,

808
00:26:43,156 --> 00:26:45,717
retirement worries or a big life change

809
00:26:45,717 --> 00:26:47,885
are more likely to take risks for

810
00:26:47,885 --> 00:26:48,739
a big payoff.

811
00:26:48,919 --> 00:26:51,009
Scammers look for those moments.

812
00:26:51,189 --> 00:26:52,733
A layoff, a divorce,

813
00:26:52,733 --> 00:26:54,354
the loss of a spouse,

814
00:26:54,354 --> 00:26:57,133
or the fear that savings won't last.

815
00:26:57,484 --> 00:26:59,306
Third, small wins.

816
00:26:59,486 --> 00:27:01,240
Many schemes let you win early.

817
00:27:01,420 --> 00:27:03,769
A small withdrawal that works,

818
00:27:03,769 --> 00:27:05,883
a first trade that profits,

819
00:27:05,883 --> 00:27:07,997
a few weeks of gains on the

820
00:27:07,997 --> 00:27:08,780
dashboard.

821
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:10,917
Those wins create confidence,

822
00:27:10,917 --> 00:27:13,616
and confidence leads to bigger deposits.

823
00:27:13,796 --> 00:27:14,841
Fourth, shame.

824
00:27:15,021 --> 00:27:16,821
Once people have lost money,

825
00:27:16,821 --> 00:27:18,236
they often keep going,

826
00:27:18,236 --> 00:27:19,651
hoping to win it back,

827
00:27:19,651 --> 00:27:22,416
or stay silent because they're embarrassed.

828
00:27:22,596 --> 00:27:23,827
Both help the scammer.

829
00:27:24,177 --> 00:27:26,487
One last thought on what actually works.

830
00:27:26,667 --> 00:27:28,873
The slow path has a hidden benefit.

831
00:27:29,053 --> 00:27:31,715
It doesn't require you to watch screens,

832
00:27:31,715 --> 00:27:33,778
chase tips, or trust strangers.

833
00:27:33,958 --> 00:27:36,378
It runs quietly in the background while

834
00:27:36,378 --> 00:27:37,556
you live your life,

835
00:27:37,556 --> 00:27:39,790
work, and spend time with people you

836
00:27:39,790 --> 00:27:40,100
love.

837
00:27:40,280 --> 00:27:42,122
A scheme asks for your money and

838
00:27:42,122 --> 00:27:42,985
your attention.

839
00:27:43,165 --> 00:27:45,421
The slow path asks only for your

840
00:27:45,421 --> 00:27:46,056
patience.

841
00:27:46,406 --> 00:27:47,588
What if it's not you,

842
00:27:47,588 --> 00:27:49,614
but someone you love who's caught in

843
00:27:49,614 --> 00:27:50,121
a scheme?

844
00:27:50,301 --> 00:27:51,369
Here's how to help,

845
00:27:51,369 --> 00:27:52,832
without pushing them away.

846
00:27:53,182 --> 00:27:54,831
Start with curiosity,

847
00:27:54,831 --> 00:27:55,852
not judgment.

848
00:27:56,032 --> 00:27:57,146
Ask questions.

849
00:27:57,326 --> 00:27:58,406
How does it make money?

850
00:27:58,586 --> 00:28:00,026
Have you been able to withdraw?

851
00:28:00,206 --> 00:28:01,645
Who else is involved?

852
00:28:01,825 --> 00:28:04,245
People defend their decisions when they feel

853
00:28:04,245 --> 00:28:04,740
attacked.

854
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:07,091
They think more clearly when they're asked

855
00:28:07,091 --> 00:28:07,660
to explain.

856
00:28:08,010 --> 00:28:09,635
Then look things up together.

857
00:28:09,815 --> 00:28:12,205
Search the company name with the word

858
00:28:12,205 --> 00:28:13,368
scam or complaint.

859
00:28:13,548 --> 00:28:16,671
Check BrokerCheck and the SEC's website.

860
00:28:16,851 --> 00:28:18,592
Look for regulator warnings.

861
00:28:18,772 --> 00:28:21,084
Finding the evidence together is much more

862
00:28:21,084 --> 00:28:23,230
powerful than being told they're wrong.

863
00:28:23,581 --> 00:28:25,113
Suggest a simple test.

864
00:28:25,293 --> 00:28:27,990
Try to withdraw a meaningful amount of

865
00:28:27,990 --> 00:28:28,416
money.

866
00:28:28,596 --> 00:28:32,025
Legitimate investments let you take your money

867
00:28:32,025 --> 00:28:33,963
out, sometimes with clear,

868
00:28:33,963 --> 00:28:36,572
disclosed fees or tax consequences.

869
00:28:36,752 --> 00:28:38,560
If withdrawals are blocked,

870
00:28:38,560 --> 00:28:40,702
delayed or require new payments,

871
00:28:40,702 --> 00:28:43,514
that's often the moment people realize the

872
00:28:43,514 --> 00:28:43,916
truth.

873
00:28:44,266 --> 00:28:45,088
And stay close,

874
00:28:45,088 --> 00:28:47,006
even if they don't listen at first.

875
00:28:47,186 --> 00:28:49,778
Many victims say they were too embarrassed

876
00:28:49,778 --> 00:28:50,889
to admit the loss.

877
00:28:51,069 --> 00:28:52,667
If they know you won't say I

878
00:28:52,667 --> 00:28:53,352
told you so,

879
00:28:53,352 --> 00:28:55,293
they're more likely to come to you

880
00:28:55,293 --> 00:28:57,234
before they send the next payment.

881
00:28:57,584 --> 00:28:59,430
Let's finish with two neighbors.

882
00:28:59,610 --> 00:29:00,759
Gary, fifty eight,

883
00:29:00,759 --> 00:29:03,505
received a friendly message from someone he

884
00:29:03,505 --> 00:29:04,207
met online.

885
00:29:04,387 --> 00:29:05,435
Over two months,

886
00:29:05,435 --> 00:29:06,744
they became friends.

887
00:29:06,924 --> 00:29:09,136
Then she showed him a crypto platform

888
00:29:09,136 --> 00:29:11,347
where she'd been earning big returns.

889
00:29:11,527 --> 00:29:13,907
Gary started with five thousand dollars.

890
00:29:14,087 --> 00:29:15,899
The app showed gains every week.

891
00:29:16,249 --> 00:29:17,396
He invested more,

892
00:29:17,396 --> 00:29:20,231
eventually much of his retirement savings.

893
00:29:20,411 --> 00:29:22,049
When he tried to withdraw,

894
00:29:22,049 --> 00:29:24,317
the platform asked for a tax payment

895
00:29:24,317 --> 00:29:24,695
first.

896
00:29:24,875 --> 00:29:25,746
Then another fee.

897
00:29:25,926 --> 00:29:27,830
Then his friend stopped answering.

898
00:29:28,010 --> 00:29:29,956
Gary lost most of what he put

899
00:29:29,956 --> 00:29:30,158
in.

900
00:29:30,338 --> 00:29:32,963
He was embarrassed and didn't tell anyone

901
00:29:32,963 --> 00:29:35,333
for months, which is very common with

902
00:29:35,333 --> 00:29:36,166
scam victims.

903
00:29:36,516 --> 00:29:37,898
His neighbor, Linda,

904
00:29:37,898 --> 00:29:39,418
got a similar message.

905
00:29:39,598 --> 00:29:40,701
But she had a rule.

906
00:29:40,881 --> 00:29:43,336
Never invest with someone I haven't met

907
00:29:43,336 --> 00:29:45,792
in person, and never through a platform

908
00:29:45,792 --> 00:29:46,988
someone else picks.

909
00:29:47,168 --> 00:29:48,818
She looked up the platform,

910
00:29:48,818 --> 00:29:50,713
found warnings about it online,

911
00:29:50,713 --> 00:29:52,241
and reported the account.

912
00:29:52,421 --> 00:29:54,216
Then she told Gary about it,

913
00:29:54,216 --> 00:29:55,690
too late for his money,

914
00:29:55,690 --> 00:29:57,484
but in time to stop him from

915
00:29:57,484 --> 00:30:00,240
paying a recovery scammer who contacted him

916
00:30:00,240 --> 00:30:00,560
next.

917
00:30:00,910 --> 00:30:02,895
The difference wasn't intelligence.

918
00:30:03,075 --> 00:30:04,476
Gary was a smart,

919
00:30:04,476 --> 00:30:05,548
educated man.

920
00:30:05,728 --> 00:30:08,021
The difference was a rule decided in

921
00:30:08,021 --> 00:30:10,441
advance, before emotions got involved.

922
00:30:10,621 --> 00:30:12,154
That's the real protection.

923
00:30:12,334 --> 00:30:14,087
Not being clever in the moment.

924
00:30:14,267 --> 00:30:16,268
Having rules that make the decision for

925
00:30:16,268 --> 00:30:16,473
you.

926
00:30:16,823 --> 00:30:19,284
Notice something else about Gary's story.

927
00:30:19,464 --> 00:30:21,378
The scam didn't feel like a scam

928
00:30:21,378 --> 00:30:22,993
at any point along the way.

929
00:30:23,173 --> 00:30:24,641
It felt like friendship,

930
00:30:24,641 --> 00:30:26,475
then like a lucky opportunity,

931
00:30:26,475 --> 00:30:28,920
then like a temporary problem with fees.

932
00:30:29,100 --> 00:30:30,331
Every step was small.

933
00:30:30,511 --> 00:30:32,810
That's how most people lose large amounts.

934
00:30:32,990 --> 00:30:34,610
Not in one big decision,

935
00:30:34,610 --> 00:30:36,568
but in a series of small ones

936
00:30:36,568 --> 00:30:38,458
that each seemed reasonable.

937
00:30:38,808 --> 00:30:40,967
Let me answer a few questions people

938
00:30:40,967 --> 00:30:42,407
ask about these schemes.

939
00:30:42,757 --> 00:30:43,546
Question one.

940
00:30:43,726 --> 00:30:45,096
Is crypto a scam?

941
00:30:45,276 --> 00:30:47,921
Crypto itself is a technology and an

942
00:30:47,921 --> 00:30:50,713
asset class, and some people invest in

943
00:30:50,713 --> 00:30:51,741
it as a small,

944
00:30:51,741 --> 00:30:54,239
high risk part of their portfolio.

945
00:30:54,419 --> 00:30:56,763
But crypto is also used in many

946
00:30:56,763 --> 00:30:59,938
scams, because transfers are fast and hard

947
00:30:59,938 --> 00:31:00,770
to reverse.

948
00:31:00,950 --> 00:31:03,164
Be very careful about who you're dealing

949
00:31:03,164 --> 00:31:05,157
with, and never invest more than you

950
00:31:05,157 --> 00:31:06,209
can afford to lose.

951
00:31:06,559 --> 00:31:07,371
Question two.

952
00:31:07,551 --> 00:31:09,827
Are all MLMs pyramid schemes?

953
00:31:10,007 --> 00:31:10,994
Not legally.

954
00:31:11,174 --> 00:31:14,030
Some sell real products to real customers.

955
00:31:14,210 --> 00:31:16,462
But many participants still lose money.

956
00:31:16,642 --> 00:31:18,337
Read the income disclosure,

957
00:31:18,337 --> 00:31:19,655
count all your costs,

958
00:31:19,655 --> 00:31:21,726
and be very cautious if the pitch

959
00:31:21,726 --> 00:31:24,174
is more about recruiting than about the

960
00:31:24,174 --> 00:31:24,676
product.

961
00:31:25,027 --> 00:31:26,060
Question three.

962
00:31:26,240 --> 00:31:28,225
What if I already lost money?

963
00:31:28,405 --> 00:31:30,283
First, stop sending money,

964
00:31:30,283 --> 00:31:32,666
no matter what fees are demanded.

965
00:31:32,846 --> 00:31:34,541
Contact your bank right away.

966
00:31:34,721 --> 00:31:37,460
Report the scam to the FTC and

967
00:31:37,460 --> 00:31:38,738
the FBI's IC3.

968
00:31:38,918 --> 00:31:41,298
Save every message and receipt.

969
00:31:41,478 --> 00:31:43,498
And talk to someone you trust.

970
00:31:43,678 --> 00:31:45,575
Shame keeps victims quiet,

971
00:31:45,575 --> 00:31:47,544
and silence helps scammers.

972
00:31:47,895 --> 00:31:48,881
Question four.

973
00:31:49,061 --> 00:31:50,710
How do I protect my parents?

974
00:31:50,890 --> 00:31:53,274
Talk about scams openly and often,

975
00:31:53,274 --> 00:31:54,466
without judgment.

976
00:31:54,646 --> 00:31:56,296
Share specific examples,

977
00:31:56,296 --> 00:31:58,152
like the wrong number text.

978
00:31:58,332 --> 00:31:59,995
Agree on a family rule:

979
00:31:59,995 --> 00:32:02,960
no big money moves without a conversation

980
00:32:02,960 --> 00:32:03,394
first.

981
00:32:03,574 --> 00:32:06,465
And consider setting up account alerts together.

982
00:32:06,815 --> 00:32:07,813
Question five.

983
00:32:07,993 --> 00:32:10,056
How can I tell a real investment

984
00:32:10,056 --> 00:32:11,604
adviser from a fake one?

985
00:32:11,784 --> 00:32:14,704
Look them up on FINRA BrokerCheck and

986
00:32:14,704 --> 00:32:18,808
the SEC's Investment Adviser Public Disclosure site.

987
00:32:18,988 --> 00:32:20,718
Ask if they're a fiduciary.

988
00:32:20,898 --> 00:32:22,697
Ask where your money will be held.

989
00:32:22,877 --> 00:32:25,654
Legitimate advisers usually use a well known

990
00:32:25,654 --> 00:32:28,747
independent custodian, a separate firm that holds

991
00:32:28,747 --> 00:32:31,146
your assets, so they can't simply take

992
00:32:31,146 --> 00:32:31,840
your money.

993
00:32:32,020 --> 00:32:33,819
If the answer is send it to

994
00:32:33,819 --> 00:32:35,352
me directly, walk away.

995
00:32:35,703 --> 00:32:36,852
Question six.

996
00:32:37,032 --> 00:32:38,890
What's the single best protection?

997
00:32:39,070 --> 00:32:40,428
A waiting period.

998
00:32:40,608 --> 00:32:42,623
Most scams depend on speed,

999
00:32:42,623 --> 00:32:44,713
because time lets you think,

1000
00:32:44,713 --> 00:32:45,832
ask and search.

1001
00:32:46,012 --> 00:32:48,568
Make a personal rule that any investment

1002
00:32:48,568 --> 00:32:50,741
over a small amount waits at least

1003
00:32:50,741 --> 00:32:53,361
one week, and gets discussed with someone

1004
00:32:53,361 --> 00:32:54,000
you trust.

1005
00:32:54,180 --> 00:32:55,805
Scammers hate that rule.

1006
00:32:55,985 --> 00:32:57,750
Honest people don't mind it at all.

1007
00:32:58,101 --> 00:32:59,424
And question seven.

1008
00:32:59,604 --> 00:33:01,479
Is there any legitimate way to get

1009
00:33:01,479 --> 00:33:02,031
rich fast?

1010
00:33:02,211 --> 00:33:04,155
Some people do get rich fast,

1011
00:33:04,155 --> 00:33:06,166
through a successful business,

1012
00:33:06,166 --> 00:33:07,574
a rare skill or luck.

1013
00:33:07,754 --> 00:33:09,396
But these are exceptions,

1014
00:33:09,396 --> 00:33:11,957
usually after years of work nobody saw.

1015
00:33:12,137 --> 00:33:13,279
For most people,

1016
00:33:13,279 --> 00:33:15,277
the reliable path is slower,

1017
00:33:15,277 --> 00:33:17,989
and it works better than any shortcut.

1018
00:33:18,339 --> 00:33:19,151
Quick recap.

1019
00:33:19,331 --> 00:33:21,579
The classics: Ponzi schemes,

1020
00:33:21,579 --> 00:33:23,426
pyramids and many MLMs,

1021
00:33:23,426 --> 00:33:26,959
the lottery, day trading and sports betting.

1022
00:33:27,139 --> 00:33:28,801
The modern hype schemes:

1023
00:33:28,801 --> 00:33:30,048
the pump and dump,

1024
00:33:30,048 --> 00:33:32,126
the mania, the trading course,

1025
00:33:32,126 --> 00:33:34,827
the free seminar and the passive income

1026
00:33:34,827 --> 00:33:35,243
dream.

1027
00:33:35,593 --> 00:33:37,710
And the internet age scams:

1028
00:33:37,710 --> 00:33:40,219
pig butchering, AI trading bots,

1029
00:33:40,219 --> 00:33:42,415
guaranteed high yield notes,

1030
00:33:42,415 --> 00:33:45,159
gifting circles and recovery scams.

1031
00:33:45,339 --> 00:33:47,034
One truth connects them all.

1032
00:33:47,214 --> 00:33:48,731
In a get rich quick scheme,

1033
00:33:48,731 --> 00:33:50,865
the person getting rich is usually the

1034
00:33:50,865 --> 00:33:51,707
one selling it.

1035
00:33:52,058 --> 00:33:53,317
If you want the real,

1036
00:33:53,317 --> 00:33:55,897
slow and reliable plan for building wealth,

1037
00:33:55,897 --> 00:33:57,096
it's in my playbook.

1038
00:33:57,276 --> 00:33:58,797
The link is in the description.

1039
00:33:58,977 --> 00:34:01,011
And watch my video on twenty money

1040
00:34:01,011 --> 00:34:02,507
myths that keep you poor.

1041
00:34:02,687 --> 00:34:04,916
Many of these schemes start with one

1042
00:34:04,916 --> 00:34:05,845
of those myths.

1043
00:34:06,025 --> 00:34:07,371
I'm Ryan Rover.

1044
00:34:07,551 --> 00:34:08,782
See you in the next one.
